# Docker build context for the control-center image.
# The context must contain exactly what `docker build` needs: no secrets, no local
# runtime state, no stale dependencies, no test files. Everything excluded here is
# either regenerated inside the image or never read by the running service.

# --- Secrets and credentials (excluded by pattern only; never read) ---
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Defense in depth for credential files that must never enter a build context.
.npmrc
**/.npmrc
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx

# --- Version control and local tooling state ---
.git
**/.git

# --- Dependencies ---
# The image runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile` itself. Host node_modules are
# stale (they still carry removed chat deps such as dompurify/marked/highlight.js)
# and `COPY . .` would drop them over the freshly installed tree.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- Local runtime state: SQLite database plus WAL/SHM sidecars ---
data
**/data
*.db*
**/*.db*

# --- Build outputs: the image rebuilds apps/web/dist; root dist/ is a release artifact ---
dist
**/dist

# --- Disposable task artifacts ---
scratch
**/scratch

# --- Maintained tests and test-only fixtures (not production inputs) ---
apps/server/src/*.test.ts
apps/server/src/**/*.test.ts
apps/web/src/*.test.ts
apps/web/src/**/*.test.ts
apps/**/src/**/fixtures
apps/**/src/**/__fixtures__

# --- Dev/release/test tooling: not a build or runtime input of the image ---
tools/test_all.sh
tools/testunit
tools

# --- Generated Python bytecode ---
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc

# --- Docs and agent skill definitions: not needed to build or run the image ---
docs
.claude
README.md

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
*.log
